  "notes": [
    "Hand compound (2026-09-02, third build). The derivation over a 24 m hall spent its eight parts on the roof and measured overshoot 0.735: a box over a 37-45 degree slope stands metres above the eaves it covers. Every roof box here has its TOP at the surface height of its OUTER edge plus the 0.30 m step (skirt 7.2 over eaves at 6.9, middle 9.0 over eaves at 9.0 on the centre section, top 10.85 over eaves 10.9, ridge 13.35 under the ridge line at hw 1.0 = 13.5), so the compound is never above the roof and the deficit inward is an undershoot, which nothing can stand on anyway. The colonnade and hall are ONE box to the skirt soffit at 6.9 over the parapet's 6.12 half-width: an exterior shell, no interior, so the columns are not walked between. The terrace and plinth boxes carry the two walkable ledges at 0.45 and 1.30; the stair box at 0.85 puts the four treads inside the step rule for a player climbing from either end. Eight parts is the hero4x ceiling; the sema stones ride on the terrace box."
